{#-
    A player's name in head metadata - title, description, unfurls (docs/features/navigation PROF-07): masked by the
    player's OWN privacy setting, never by the viewer. An allowed friend sees the name on the page, but their browser
    must not emit an indexable or unfurlable identity for a private profile; the player sees their own name.

    Prints PLAIN TEXT, not HTML (escaping happens where it is printed): take it only as
    `include('player/_head_name.html.twig', {player: player})|trim` - the filter makes it a string Twig escapes once,
    e.g. inside a translation parameter. Never print the include itself.

    Input: player (PlayerProfile)
-#}
{%- autoescape false -%}
    {%- set is_own = logged_user.profile is not null and logged_user.profile.playerId is same as player.playerId -%}
    {{- player.isPrivateProfile and not is_own
        ? ('secret_puzzler_name'|trans ~ ' #' ~ player.code|upper)
        : (player.playerName ?? ('#' ~ player.code|upper)) -}}
{%- endautoescape -%}
